  "description": "The Archer points his arrow toward the heart of the Milky Way, making this the richest region of the night sky for star clusters, nebulae, and deep-sky objects. Looking toward Sagittarius means looking toward the Galactic centre, about 26,000 light-years away — where Sgr A*, the Milky Way's supermassive black hole, resides.",
